    {
      "id": "claim_bd47517036e844bfa5670efeecc904e7",
      "statement": "The agent-facing observability session funnels every read through one #observe wrapper that records the read on the approval queue before returning it, so a read that reaches the agent but not the queue would be an unaudited disclosure; filter values are kept out of audit entries via summarizeFilter so a queue entry cannot become an exfiltration channel.",
      "evidence": [
